{
  "_comment": [
    "J6 target calibration records: one per measured target, each the evidence a frozen",
    "EncodingCostTable was built from. bcir/asn1/calibration.py decides admissibility;",
    "tools/silicon/measure_asn1_calibration.sh produces a record on a declared target.",
    "",
    "Every record must carry the same `corpus` digest and the same `method`: two targets",
    "measured against different schemas, or timed different ways, produce two tables that",
    "look identical, compare cleanly, and mean nothing.",
    "",
    "steal_ticks/throttled_usec are null on Android, where /proc/stat is restricted, and",
    "`counters` reads 'Permission denied' because Android denies perf_event_open. Null means",
    "UNREPORTED, not zero -- the reader declines to refuse on a counter nobody could read.",
    "",
    "The two records below are the SAME PHONE on different core clusters, and that is the",
    "point rather than a duplicate: a Cortex-X4 and a Cortex-A520 are different machines, and",
    "the A520 is roughly 4-5x slower on every candidate. Averaging them would describe no core",
    "that exists, which is what the multi-CPU refusal prevents."
  ],
